<title>INDIA: Indian Aug 24-sector industrial output up 4.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Indian Aug 24-sector industrial output up 4.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's 24-sector industrial production index rose 4.4 percent in August over the same month in 1995, the Industry Ministry said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>    24-SECTOR INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION   Aug 96	 Apr-Aug 96</p>
<p>    Coal					 +2.2	    +8.9</p>
<p>    Crude petroleum			 -11.8	   -10.4</p>
<p>    Cement				    +14.9	   +13.8</p>
<p>    Saleable steel			   +2.1	    +4.6</p>
<p>    Electricity generation		 +2.2	    +2.4</p>
<p>    Petroleum refinery products	 +15.6	    +7.3</p>
<p>    Steel ingots			     +5.7	    +4.2</p>
<p>    Nitrogenous fertiliser		 +6.8	    -7.7</p>
<p>    Phosphatic fertiliser		  -1.1	   -11.6</p>
<p>    Saleable pig iron		     +29.6	   +18.3</p>
<p>    Aluminium				  +1.2	    -4.3</p>
<p>    Copper cathodes			 -44.7	   -34.9</p>
<p>    Sugar				     -18.3	   +59.1</p>
<p>    Salt					 +0.0	    +7.7</p>
<p>    Cloth-mill sector		     +14.1	   +16.2</p>
<p>    Cloth-decentralised sector	   +7.2	    +6.5</p>
<p>    Cotton yarn			     +12.5	    +7.9</p>
<p>    Jute manufacturers		    -30.1	   -14.4</p>
<p>    Commercial vehicles		    +8.1	   +18.5</p>
<p>    Cars					+13.6	   +21.6</p>
<p>    Jeeps				    +101.9	   +28.8</p>
<p>    Motor cycles			    +27.3	   +26.8</p>
<p>    Auto rickshaws			  +35.6	   +43.5</p>
<p>    Scooters/mopeds			 +28.6	   +24.0</p>
<p>    OVERALL				    +4.4	    +5.6</p>
<p>Note - The index includes 24 sectors accounting for 50.4 percent of the overall index of industrial production. The figures are preliminary.</p>
</text>
